  "message": "Good news: the local emulation of revision 2 passed with no failures or gaps. That means the generated code ran correctly against simulated AWS services for retrieval, permission filtering and cited answers. It doesn't verify real sign-in, IAM, API routing, Bedrock answer quality or deployment, so we don't need a diagram change. What matters most now is the boundary we haven't tested, and the region depends on where the data is allowed to live. Which country does this synthetic data need to stay in? With that, we can propose an AWS region and check which Bedrock model is available there for a real validation.",
